<Project>

	<!--
	Cross-platform RID set. The portable engine (Core/Infrastructure/Services) and the headless
	host target net10.0 and run on every RID below; the WinForms tray host and module UI build
	only for win-* (WindowsDesktop framework). Native assets (LibGit2Sharp, OnnxRuntime,
	SQLitePCLRaw, sqlite-vec) all ship linux-x64/arm64 and osx-x64/arm64.

	No global RuntimeIdentifier(s) is set: everyday build/test stays framework-dependent with
	unchanged output paths. To target another platform, publish the portable projects with an
	explicit RID, e.g. `dotnet publish -r osx-arm64` (linux-x64 = glibc; use linux-musl-x64 for
	Alpine). A plural RuntimeIdentifiers list here would force every project — including the
	Windows-only host — to restore runtime packs for all RIDs and fail (NETSDK1082).
	-->

</Project>
